# ── www canonicalization — ACTION NEEDED IN CLOUDFLARE DASHBOARD ──────────
# astro.config.mjs (site:) and every SEO schema/sitemap in this codebase
# treat https://www.packershub.in as the one canonical domain (fixed in
# v10.7.13 — SITE_URL and the AI voice agent's hardcoded URLs were pointing
# at the non-www form, which didn't match). This _redirects file is
# PATH-based only — Cloudflare Pages cannot condition a rule on hostname
# here, so a non-www -> www redirect cannot be added in this file.
# One-time manual step: Cloudflare dashboard -> your zone (packershub.in) ->
# Rules -> Redirect Rules -> create a rule matching hostname = packershub.in
# (no www) -> redirect to https://www.packershub.in/${path} (301, preserve
# query string). Without this, Google can index both packershub.in and
# www.packershub.in as separate, competing pages.

